        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ముంచెత్తు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ముంచెత్తు — muñcettu — \"to inundate; to flood\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "వరద నీరు గ్రామాన్ని ముంచెత్తింది. varada nīru grāmānni muñcettindi. The floodwater inundated the village."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ముంచెత్తాను, muñcettānu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ముంచు, to dip, + ఎత్తు, to lift: to plunge under. Also said of a crowd or of gifts: పూలతో ముంచెత్తారు."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ముంచెత్తు (muñcettu) is native Dravidian: ముంచు, \"to plunge, to immerse\" (DEDR 4993), and ఎత్తు, \"to lift, to raise\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
