              "text": "తెగిపోవు — tegipōvu — \"to snap; to be cut off\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "వరదలో రోడ్డు తెగిపోయింది. varadalō rōḍḍu tegipōyindi. The road was cut off in the flood."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (it …): తెగిపోయింది, tegipōyindi."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Said of a rope, a wire, a road or a bond that breaks apart. Its subject is a thing, so the past shown is the third person: తెగిపోయింది, it snapped."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "తెగిపోవు (tegipōvu) is a Telugu compound: తెగు, \"to break off, to be cut\", whose origin is not settled, and the native పోవు, \"to go\" (DEDR 4572)."
            }
          ]
